title: Works Council Elections
subtitle: The vote at one of the great works.
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: {!
if (typeof RG === 'undefined') { return false; }
if (!RG.lw && this.game.scenes.lw_lib) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
return !!(RG.lw && RG.lw.ready('council_election'));
!}
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
RG.lw.fire('council_election');
// our chance in a free vote: the district's mood and the party's standing
Q.lw_n = RG.clamp(0.15 + RG.num(Q['district_' + Q.lw_d + '_militancy']) / 200 + RG.num(Q.worker_support) / 150, 0.15, 0.85);
Q.lw_amount = Q.lw_n >= 0.55 ? 1 : 0;
!}

= Works Council Elections

At **[+ lw_works +]**, in [+ lw_d_name +], the ballot boxes stand in the canteen for three days, guarded by a social democratic shop steward and one of ours, who do not speak to each other. The council cannot run the works, but it can see the books and defend a sacked man, and the workforce listens to whoever wins it.

[? if lw_amount = 1 : Our people think a red list could win. ?][? if lw_amount = 0 : Our people think a red list would lose. ?]

- @red: Stand a red list of our own.
- @joint: Stand a joint list with the left of the other parties.
- @union: Put our people on the union's list.

@red
subtitle: All or nothing. A win makes the works ours.
on-arrival: {!
if (Math.random() < Q.lw_n) {
    Q.lw_out = 1;
    RG.district(Q.lw_d, {members: 0.08, loyalty: 6});
    RG.news('Red list wins the works council at ' + Q.lw_works.replace(/^the /, ''), 2);
    RG.ledger('Communists won the works council at ' + Q.lw_works + '.', 'lw_council_first');
} else {
    Q.lw_out = 2;
    Q.worker_support -= 2;
}
!}

[? if lw_out = 1 : The red list takes the majority. On Monday the new chairman walks into the director's office and asks to see the order books. ?][? if lw_out = 2 : The red list wins a third of the seats. The social democrats keep the chair. ?]

@joint
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A likely win, and a shared one.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids joint lists with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('united_front');
if (Math.random() < Q.lw_n + 0.25) {
    Q.lw_out = 1;
    RG.district(Q.lw_d, {members: 0.03});
    Q.uspd_relation += 4;
} else {
    Q.lw_out = 2;
}
Q.spd_relation += 4;
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 2, 5);
!}

[? if lw_out = 1 : The joint list wins easily. The chair goes to an Independent and the deputy chair to one of ours. ?][? if lw_out = 2 : Even together the left loses to the Christian union and the foremen's list. ?]

@union
subtitle: [? if lock_union_work = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] No fight with the union. Three of ours at the bottom of its list.
choose-if: lock_union_work < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids working inside the reformist unions.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('union_work');
Q.worker_support += 2;
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 1, 3);
!}

All three are elected.
